<div style="border: 2px solid #1a5276; padding: 15px; text-align: center; background-color: #e0f2f7;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # I Can Make a Mola. – Lesson # 2</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 2</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Reading</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 4th Grade (CEFR: A1.2)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> The Beautiful Mola</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> I Can Make a Mola.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Reading: reading1: Respond creatively to stories read. reading2: Summarize simple stories or articles. phonemicAwareness: Read regularly spelled one-syllable or two-syllable words represented by single letters.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Reading: Can respond creatively by identifying colors and shapes in stories about molas (e.g., 'red, blue, round.'). Can summarize a short text about mola art, mentioning key ideas (e.g., 'Molas have bright colors.'). Can spell and read one-syllable or two-syllable words using phonemic awareness and alphabet knowledge related to colors and instructions (e.g., 'orange,' 'vibrant,' and 'square').</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e0f2f7; color: #1a5276; width: 30%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e0f2f7; color: #1a5276; width: 50%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #e0f2f7; color: #1a5276; width: 20%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher shows pictures of different molas (realia or flashcards). Students identify colors, shapes, and animals they see. Teacher asks: "What colors do you see?" (e.g., 'red,' 'blue,' 'yellow,' 'orange,' 'turquoise,' 'golden'). "What shapes do you see?" (e.g., 'round,' 'square'). "What animals do you see?" (e.g., 'turtle,' 'butterfly,' 'jaguar'). Students respond with single words or short phrases. This connects to prior vocabulary from Lesson 1.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher holds up a picture of a mola and says, "This is a mola. A mola has many vibrant colors. It has a round shape. I see a butterfly." The teacher models the pronunciation of 'mola' (/m/) and 'colors' (/k/) clearly. The teacher then models reading simple sentences aloud, pointing to each word: "Molas are art. They are beautiful."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is a mola an animal or art?" (Expected: "Art!")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Do molas have one color or many colors?" (Expected: "Many colors!")</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short, illustrated descriptive text titled "Making a Mola." The text will incorporate target vocabulary (mola, vibrant, colors, shapes, cut, sew, paste, choose, first, second, third, because, turtle, butterfly, jaguar) and grammar (present simple, 'because,' instructional steps). The genre is a simple informative narrative excerpt about mola art creation steps.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Students will comprehend the main ideas and specific details in a simple written text about molas.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Text Example:</b><br/>
                    "Hello! My name is Ana. I like to make molas. A mola is special art from the Guna people. It has many vibrant colors like red, blue, and golden. Molas often have round or square shapes. You can see animals like a turtle, a butterfly, or a jaguar on a mola. I like this mola because it has a big, round turtle. Making a mola is fun! First, you choose your colors. Second, you carefully cut the fabric. Third, you sew the pieces. It’s a creative project!"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Question (Teacher reads aloud, students listen):</b> "What is this story about?" (Expected: "Molas," "Making art.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False (Teacher reads statements, students say True or False):</b>
                        <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Molas have many vibrant colors." (True)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Molas have square and round shapes." (True)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"You can see a dog on a mola." (False)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10-12 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Reading)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Reading comprehension, identifying key details, understanding instructional steps, using 'because' for reasons. Vocabulary: mola, creativity, project, turtle, butterfly, jaguar, cut, sew, paste, choose, express, illustrate, decorate, collaborate, turquoise, golden, round, vibrant, traditional, unique, carefully, skillfully, artistically, first, second, third, next, last. Grammar: Present simple ('A mola has...'), 'because,' instructional steps. Phonemic Awareness: Spelling one-syllable or two-syllable words (e.g., 'red,' 'orange,' 'vibrant,' 'second'). Pragmatic: Describing things ('A mola has many colors.').</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. <b>Controlled Practice - "Find and Match":</b>
                        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher provides a worksheet with sentences from the text and blanks. Below the blanks are target vocabulary words (e.g., 'vibrant,' 'turtle,' 'cut,' 'first'). Students read the text again to find the missing words and write them in the blanks. Example: "Molas have many _______ colors." (vibrant). "You can see a _______ or a butterfly." (turtle). "_______, you choose your colors." (First). Teacher emphasizes spelling and reading these words using phonemic awareness (e.g., 'vibrant', 'second').</p>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. <b>Semi-Controlled Practice - "Sequence the Steps":</b>
                        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher writes the mola-making steps from the text on separate strips of paper (e.g., "Sew the pieces," "Choose your colors," "Cut the fabric"). Students work in small groups. They read the strips and reorder them correctly according to the text (First, Second, Third...). Teacher monitors, providing support to ensure accurate reading of the instructional language.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. <b>Pair Interaction - "Read and Ask":</b>
                        <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in pairs. Partner A reads a sentence from the text (e.g., "I like this mola because it has a big, round turtle."). Partner B asks a simple question about it (e.g., "Why does Ana like the mola?"). Partner A answers using 'because.' They switch roles. This activity encourages reading aloud and checks comprehension of simple facts and reasons, promoting sociolinguistic interaction.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">15-18 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative "My Favorite Mola" drawing and short oral description.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in small groups (3-4 students). Each group receives a large sheet of paper and drawing materials (crayons, markers). Their task is to collaboratively draw "My Favorite Mola" inspired by the story they read. They must include at least two colors, one shape, and one animal mentioned in the text (e.g., 'red,' 'blue,' 'round,' 'butterfly'). As they draw, they should talk about their choices using learned vocabulary and grammar (e.g., "Let's choose blue," "A mola has many colors," "I like the turtle because it is round.").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">After drawing, each group takes turns presenting their mola to the class. One student from each group reads aloud a sentence summarizing a key idea from the text (e.g., "Molas have bright colors. This is a traditional art."). Another student describes their group's mola, stating why they chose certain elements (e.g., "We chose a golden butterfly because it is unique. Our mola has a square shape because we like it."). This activity allows them to respond creatively to the story read and summarize simple aspects while expressing preferences.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">10-12 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy and student reflection)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during group work and presentations. Peer assessment during presentations.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students present their collaborative mola drawing and verbally summarize 1-2 key facts from the text and describe their choices using 'because'. They also provide peer feedback.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria (Teacher checklist and Peer Feedback):</b></p>
                <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation of /m/ in 'mola' and /k/ in 'colors', and target vocabulary.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of target vocabulary (e.g., 'vibrant,' 'turtle,' 'round,' 'because,' 'first') from the lesson.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity in describing their mola and expressing preferences ("I like this mola because...").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Ability to summarize a simple fact from the text (e.g., "Molas have many colors.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Participation in collaborative art-making and acknowledging peers' contributions.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket (written or verbal):</b></p>
                <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one new word you learned about molas today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What did you like about reading the mola story?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">5-7 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What did I learn about molas today from reading?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of reading about molas was easy? What was difficult?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul style="margin-top: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this reading lesson? (e.g., students engaged with the text, correctly identified key details, used 'because' effectively).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for next time? (e.g., more visual support for vocabulary, simpler text structure, additional guided reading practice).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Did students successfully summarize simple aspects and respond creatively?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This lesson focused on reading about molas and their creation. The next lesson (Lesson 3: Speaking & Interaction) will build on this knowledge by having students actively speak and interact about molas, using the same vocabulary and grammar to express preferences and describe their mola creations orally in pairs and groups.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">3-5 min</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>